# ⚡ Using this repo to improve a USER's UI/site (most common)
A user wants you to improve THEIR project, using this repo as a design knowledge base:
1. Read CONSULT.md and follow its steps in order (classify input → audit → knowledge files → preset → generate → Design Review Notes).
2. Start from a preset. Enumerate available templates from docs/presets/index.json (machine-readable source of truth). Customize a preset; do NOT build components from scratch.
3. Always produce Design Review Notes (CONSULT.md Step 4) — the primary deliverable.
4. Match the user's stack. Default to HTML + Tailwind only when the stack is unknown.
5. Do NOT edit or "improve" THIS repo — apply all changes to the USER's project.

# 🔧 Maintaining this repo
See MAINTAINING.md.

# References
Read CONSULT.md for the full design consultation workflow.
Enumerate ALL templates from docs/presets/index.json (authoritative list); read docs/presets/_index.md for composition recipes.
The #preset:{element}/{personality} GitHub Pages URLs are human-preview-only — headless agents can't open them; read preset HTML files directly.
Read workflows/quick-reference.md for critical design numbers.
Match the user's tech stack — don't output Tailwind HTML to someone using React + styled-components.
Always generate Design Review Notes (Step 4 in CONSULT.md) as the primary deliverable.
